From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 00:09:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Actually apply the shared radial scale, and add SNR 100

The shared scale in the previous commit had no visible effect: every glyph
was still drawn the same size. Scaling the radius was correct but got thrown
away at draw time.

axis equal fixes a panel's ASPECT RATIO, not its LIMITS. Left alone, MATLAB
autoscales each subplot to its own data, so a glyph half the size of its
neighbour gets an axis range half as wide and lands on the page at exactly
the same size. The edema response really was being drawn at 1/3 the radius
and then magnified back to fill its panel.

Fixed by pinning every 3D panel to GLYPH_LIM = [-1.02 1.02] after scaling
each glyph so its maximum radius is at most 1. Both halves are needed;
either alone does nothing. All six glyph draw sites are pinned.

Two scales were wrong in the same way and are fixed too:

  * Figures 4 and 5 drew fODFs at scale 1 with autoscaled limits, so a
    flatter reconstruction looked identical to a sharp one. They now share
    one scale computed across the truth and every fODF both figures draw,
    so healthy and edema are comparable and a flatter fit looks flatter.
  * Figure 1's ground truth is an fODF, not a signal. It is deliberately NOT
    on the response scale -- the two are different quantities and sharing a
    scale between them would mean nothing -- so it is normalised to its own
    peak and the file says why.

SNR_LIST gains 100, matching the local run: [5 10 20 30 50 100 Inf]. That
takes the sweep to 42 fits, 7 SNR x 3 Lmax x 2 kernels.

No simulation was run. The figure block was re-executed against the
graphics stubs. Note that the stubs make set(gca,...) a no-op, so what is
verified is that the code runs, not that the pinning renders -- that is the
part that needs eyes on a real MATLAB figure, and it is exactly what the
previous commit got wrong.

